# The device target contract, in ONE place.
#
# Every value below is a property of the Debian suite the CeraLive device image
# ships, so they move together or not at all. A suite flip edits this file and
# nothing else: the build matrix's TARGET leg runs in `debian:${TARGET_SUITE}-slim`,
# the GLIBC gate (check-glibc-floor.sh) rejects any import above
# GLIBC_${GLIBC_FLOOR}, and GST_RUNTIME_MINOR is the GStreamer minor that suite
# actually ships.
#
# GST_RUNTIME_MINOR is NOT an independent pin — it is a fact about TARGET_SUITE
# (bookworm ships 1.22, trixie ships 1.26). The build matrix declares its suite
# legs statically and asserts, per leg, that the suite/minor pair it was handed
# agrees with this file for the target leg. That assertion is the whole point of
# spelling the minor here: it fails a build rather than letting the two drift.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: any GStreamer minor in `debian/control`. This plugin
# builds against >= 1.14 and must keep resolving on both 1.22 and 1.26; a
# versioned Depends would pin the package to one runtime it has no reason to
# require.
TARGET_SUITE=bookworm
GLIBC_FLOOR=2.36
GST_RUNTIME_MINOR=1.22
